# ── How to hand the fetcher your already-solved session ───────────────────
#
# The script drives Brave with its OWN profile, which is a different cookie
# jar from the Brave you browse in. That is why solving the CAPTCHA in your
# normal window does not help it. Paste your solved session here instead.
#
# STEPS
#   1. In normal Brave, open:
#        https://erecruitment.bb.org.bd/career/jobopportunity.php
#      Solve the CAPTCHA if one appears, until you SEE the notice table.
#   2. Press F12  →  Network tab  →  press F5 to reload.
#   3. Click the FIRST row (jobopportunity.php).
#   4. Right-click it → Copy → "Copy as cURL (bash)".
#   5. Paste the whole thing below, save this file as  session.txt
#      (remove the .example from the filename).
#   6. Run run.bat as usual.
#
# ANY of these Copy-as formats work — pick whichever you clicked:
#      Copy as cURL (bash)      Copy as cURL (cmd)
#      Copy as fetch            Copy as fetch (Node.js)
#      Copy as PowerShell
# Modern Brave/Chrome write the cookie as   -b $'PHPSESSID=...; TSPD_101=...'
# rather than a cookie: header; both are understood, and the \u0021 escapes
# bash adds are decoded back to ! before the cookie is used.
# Or write the cookie line yourself:
#      cookie: TSPD_101=...; bb_cookie=...; TS01cf43c8=...
#
# TO CHECK IT WORKED, before running a full fetch:
#      session-check.bat
# It prints the cookie NAMES only (never the values), so the output is safe
# to share. You want TSPD_101 in that list.
#
# ⚠  This file is a LIVE LOGIN. .gitignore already excludes session.txt, so it
#    will not reach GitHub — but never paste its contents into a chat or issue.
#    It expires on its own, usually within hours to a few days; when the fetch
#    starts failing again, just repeat the steps above.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

